---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL, SITE_URL, LAST_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS, GA4_ID, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { label } from '../../i18n/nav';
import { facts } from '../../lib/facts';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const F = facts(lang);
const updated = displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS[lang]);
const tools = [GA4_ID && 'Google Analytics 4', CLARITY_ID && 'Microsoft Clarity'].filter(Boolean).join(' and ');
const title = `Privacy Policy ${F.year}: Calculations Stay in Your Browser`;
const description = `GDPR in practice: in ${F.year} the salaries you type never leave your device. What our hosting provider sees, how long we keep emails, your rights over your data.`;
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} noindex={true}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: label('home', lang), path: route('home', lang) }, { name: label('privacy', lang), path: route('privacy', lang) }])]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: label('privacy', lang) }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">In short: the calculators send your figures nowhere{tools ? '' : ', and the site uses no cookies, no audience measurement and no advertising'}. Below are the details the General Data Protection Regulation (EU Regulation 2016/679) requires for {SITE_URL}.</p>

    <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>For data protection matters, write to the same address: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. No data protection officer has been appointed, as the GDPR does not require one at this scale of processing.</p>

    <h2>2. The calculators send nothing</h2>
    <p>Every calculation runs in your browser. Your salary, children, age, car or property details are <strong>not transmitted to any server</strong>, not stored and not linked to any identifier. There are no accounts and no sign-up.</p>
    <p>One thing worth knowing: after you change a field, the calculator writes the values into the page address so you can share a ready-made calculation. That link contains your figures, your salary for instance, and remains in your browser history, so only send it to people you want to see them.</p>

    <h2>3. What is actually processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting provider logs</h3>
    <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Like any server, it receives the visitor’s IP address and technical request data on every visit; according to <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">GitHub’s documentation</a>, visitors’ IP addresses are logged and stored for security purposes. We have no access to those logs and do not use them. The legal basis is legitimate interest (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)): serving the page and protecting it from abuse. GitHub sets the retention period in its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy statement</a>.</p>
    <h3>Emails</h3>
    <p>If you write to us, we process your address and message to reply and, where needed, to correct a calculation (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)). We keep correspondence for no more than three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h3>Audience measurement and advertising</h3>
    {tools
      ? <p>The site may use {tools} to measure traffic, <strong>only after you accept it</strong> in the consent banner; without acceptance nothing is loaded. Your choice is kept on your device and can be changed from the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>. The values you type into the calculators are not passed to these tools either. There is no advertising.</p>
      : <p>Today the site <strong>uses no audience measurement tool</strong> (no Google Analytics, no Microsoft Clarity, nothing else) and <strong>shows no advertising</strong>. It loads no fonts or scripts from other domains.</p>}

    <h2>4. Who receives data</h2>
    <p>We do not sell, rent or share personal data for marketing. The only recipient of technical data is the hosting provider; emails pass through our mail provider, which processes them on our behalf.</p>

    <h2>5. Transfers outside the European Economic Area</h2>
    <p>GitHub, Inc. is based in the United States, so technical request data may be processed outside the EEA. GitHub describes in its privacy statement the GDPR transfer mechanisms it relies on.</p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection to processing based on legitimate interest (GDPR arts. 15 to 21). Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we answer free of charge within one month. As we keep no user accounts, we usually hold nothing that identifies you beyond any correspondence, and we will tell you so plainly.</p>
    <p>You may also complain to a supervisory authority. The controller is established in France, so the lead authority is the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>). If you live in Greece you can also turn to the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.dpa.gr" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">dpa.gr</a>), under GDPR article 77.</p>

    <h2>7. No profiling</h2>
    <p>A calculator result is an operation you request, carried out on your device with your own data. It has no legal effect and is not an automated decision within the meaning of GDPR article 22. We build no user profiles.</p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>Before switching on any audience measurement or advertising, we first update this page and the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>. Where the law requires consent, you will be asked before anything is stored on your device. The connection to the site is encrypted (HTTPS) and no user database is kept. The terms of use are <a href={route('terms', lang)}>here</a>, and the code to embed the calculator is on the <a href={route('widget', lang)}>widget page</a>.</p>
    <p>Version of {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
